<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The New Zealand Expo Song (Alan Slater)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1987</span><span class="sg-chain-h">bilingual arrangement made for Expo 88</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Arrangement for massed singing (Maxwell Fernie)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1979</span><span class="sg-chain-h">official alternative arrangement, a semitone lower</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Aotearoa (Thomas Henry Smith)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1878</span><span class="sg-chain-h">Māori version, not a direct translation</span></li></ul></section>
<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired-by"><h2>What it drew on</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">God Defend New Zealand, poem (Thomas Bracken)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1870s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">the poem set to music in 1876</span></li></ul></section>
